    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, our company's has experience in managing large-scale projects, with a largest project managed worth 4.5 million euros, which is within the budget range of The City of Belval global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years.  our company's has also demonstrated expertise in public sector IT and digital transformation, having completed 23 public sector projects as of 2024, including a digital workplace transformation for Comune di Torino and an AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia. our company's can leverage our company's consortium experience, having led 8 consortia with up to 5 partners, to assemble a team that meets the requirements. Notably, our company's known partner EuroCloud Solutions S.A. has expertise in sovereign cloud hosting and SecNumCloud infrastructure, which aligns with the constraint of hosting data exclusively on European Union territory. our company's project management capabilities include PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies, ensuring our company's can adapt to The City of Belval needs. our company's also have a dedicated change manager and training delivery capabilities to support user adoption and minimize disruption. Given our company's available PM capacity is 60% as of 2024, with the next available start date being March 1, 2025, our company's would need to assess if this aligns with this project timelines." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, based on the information provided, it appears our company's has the necessary expertise, experience, and capabilities to assemble a team that can meet The City of Belval requirements and constraints for improving administrative services efficiency, reducing environmental footprint, and minimizing energetic consumption within the specified budget." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has experience in managing large-scale projects, with a largest project managed worth 4.5 million euros, which is within the budget range of the City of Belval's global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has also demonstrated expertise in public sector IT and digital transformation, having completed 23 public sector projects as of 2024, including a digital workplace transformation for Comune di Torino and an AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can leverage Nexus Engineering S.r.l. consortium experience, having led 8 consortia with up to 5 partners, to assemble a team that meets the requirements. Notably, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. known partner EuroCloud Solutions S.A. has expertise in sovereign cloud hosting and SecNumCloud infrastructure, which aligns with the constraint of hosting data exclusively on European Union territory. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. project management capabilities include PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies, ensuring Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can adapt to the City of Belval's needs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message4> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also have a dedicated change manager and training delivery capabilities to support user adoption and minimize disruption. Given Nexus Engineering S.r.l. available PM capacity is 60% as of 2024, with the next available start date being March 1, 2025, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. would need to assess if this aligns with the project's timelines. However, based on the information provided, it appears Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has the necessary expertise, experience, and capabilities to assemble a team that can meet the City of Belval's requirements and constraints for improving administrative services efficiency, reducing environmental footprint, and minimizing energetic consumption within the specified budget. Based on the provided context, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has experience in managing public sector projects, having completed 23 public sector projects, which includes digital transformation and public sector IT sectors that could be relevant to improving administrative services efficiency and quality of service rendered to users. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also has consortium experience, having led consortia with partners such as our known partner EuroCloud Solutions S.A., who has expertise in sovereign cloud hosting and SecNumCloud infrastructure, which might help in reducing environmental footprint by leveraging green IT solutions, potentially including energy-efficient infrastructure through Nexus Engineering S.r.l. known partner GreenCompute S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message4> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have project management capabilities that include PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies. However, I do not have specific information on how project management capabilities that include PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies directly address the reduction of environmental footprint or energetic consumption beyond Nexus Engineering S.r.l. general expertise in digital transformation and IT. Regarding available capacity, I know that as of 2024, we have 60% available PM capacity, but I do not have information on whether 60% available PM capacity is sufficient for a project of the specified budget and duration without more details on a project of the specified budget and duration requirements. I do not have explicit information on how our governance practices or past references directly address minimizing energetic consumption or ensuring annual costs of exploitation remain compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities. Therefore, while Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have relevant experience and capabilities in public sector IT and digital transformation, I cannot confirm with certainty that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can assemble a team meeting all the specified requirements and constraints without additional information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message4> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution requires integration with existing systems of information (business softwares, electronic management of documents, user directories), API integration, response time < 2 seconds, 99.9% availability, and hosting on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, with no dependency on non-European suppliers. Can our current technology stack meet these technical requirements, and what architecture do our propose? Based on our context, our can address several of these technical requirements. For integration with existing systems of information, our experience with API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, along with our proficiency in using API gateways like Kong and Apigee, can facilitate integration with existing systems of information. Additionally, our familiarity with identity providers like Active Directory/LDAP and Keycloak can help with user directory integration." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For the electronic management of documents, our experience with GED systems such as Alfresco, Maarch Courrier, and OpenKM can be beneficial. our also have expertise in ERP/CRM connectors for systems like SAP, Salesforce, Oracle, Ciril/ARPÈGE, and OXALIS, which covers business software integration. Regarding response time and availability, our performance benchmarks indicate a p95 response time of 1800 ms for RAG ( Retrieval-Augmented Generation) tasks, which is below the 2-second threshold. However, a p95 response time of 1800 ms for RAG ( Retrieval-Augmented Generation) tasks, which is below the 2-second threshold is specific to RAG tasks and may vary depending on the overall system design and workload. our typical availability achieved on past projects is 99.92%, exceeding the required 99.9% availability. For hosting, our experience with cloud providers includes OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale (SecNumCloud), all of which are European and can meet the sovereignty requirement. Specifically, deploying on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU aligns with our capabilities, ensuring no dependency on non-European suppliers for critical components." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given these requirements, I propose an architecture that leverages our strengths in API integration, cloud deployment on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, and expertise in document management and identity providers. an architecture that leverages our strengths in API integration, cloud deployment on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, and expertise in document management and identity providers would involve designing a microservices-based system where each component (e.g., document management, business software integration, user authentication) is developed as an independent service communicating through APIs.  an architecture that leverages our strengths in API integration, cloud deployment on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, and expertise in document management and identity providers allows for flexible scalability, meeting the availability requirement by ensuring that if one service experiences downtime, others can continue to operate. Utilizing containerization with Docker and orchestration with Kubernetes can further enhance scalability and reliability. To meet the availability requirement, our would need to optimize database queries, ensure efficient API call handling, and possibly implement caching mechanisms where appropriate. Monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana can be used to track performance metrics and quickly identify bottlenecks. While our technology stack and experience can meet many of the specified technical requirements, careful planning, testing, and optimization will be necessary to ensure that all requirements are fully satisfied, especially those related to response time and availability in a production environment." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only hosting, no data transfer outside EU, encryption of sensitive data), explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued by the solution, and a high level of security. Considering our company's certifications, GDPR instruments, AI security controls, audit capabilities, and experience with EU regulatory frameworks as of 2024, are our company's compliant with these requirements, and what measures do our company's need to take to ensure compliance? Based on our company's company context, our company's have the necessary certifications and instruments to comply with these requirements. our company's hold ISO 27001 certification, which includes the scope of Design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, and our company's have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed, who can be contacted at dpo@nexus-engineering.it. our company's standard data residency is EU-only, and our company's cross-border transfer policy prohibits transfers outside EU unless there is an explicit legal basis. our company's also have measures in place for anonymization of sensitive data, using tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our company's have implemented data subject rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection. For explicability and transparency, our company's AI security controls include output PII redaction, confidence threshold escalation, and model update security review. However, our company's do not have explicit information on providing explanations for recommendations or proposals issued by the solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address this, our company's would need to implement additional measures, such as providing documentation or logging of the decision-making process. In terms of security, our company's have a high level of security controls in place, including multi-factor authentication (MFA) enforced with TOTP and hardware token (FIDO2), Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) design experience, and Privileged Access Management (PAM) solutions such as CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault. our company's also have a Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) system in place, with real-time integration and log immutability using SHA-256 hash chaining. To ensure compliance with these requirements, our company's should review our company's existing measures to ensure our existing measures are up-to-date and aligned with the latest regulatory frameworks. our company's should also consider implementing additional measures to address explicability and transparency, such as providing documentation or logging of the decision-making process." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, our company's should conduct regular audits and risk assessments to identify potential vulnerabilities and ensure that our company's security controls are effective." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires contractual compliance with the City of Belval's regulatory requirements, a level of security, and global cost of the solution. Considering our company's legal standing, procurement experience across EU jurisdictions, IP model, insurance, standard contractual clauses, and AI regulatory posture as of 2024, what are the potential legal risks associated with this project, and how can our company's mitigate the potential legal risks associated with this project? Based on the provided context, the potential legal risks associated with this project include compliance with the City of Belval's regulatory requirements, data protection, intellectual property, liability, and insurance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message10> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To mitigate the potential legal risks associated with this project, our company's can rely on our company's experience in public procurement across EU jurisdictions, including France where the City of Belval's is located. our company's has experience with the French Code Commande Publique, which could be beneficial in navigating local regulatory requirements. Regarding data protection, our company's GDPR compliance measures, including a Data Protection Agreement template (v3.2), standard legal basis under Article 6(1)(e) for processing personal data, and DPIA support availability, can help mitigate risks associated with data processing. In terms of intellectual property, our company's default IP model is work-for-hire, which transfers all deliverables to the client upon final payment, minimizing potential disputes over ownership." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message10> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our company's source code escrow capability through Logitas (France where the City of Belval is located) provides an added layer of security for both parties. Liability and insurance risks can be mitigated by our company's professional indemnity insurance coverage of 5 million euros, cyber liability insurance of 2 million euros, and a limitation of liability standard of 3 million euros. our company's performance bond capacity of 1.5 million euros further ensures the client's interests are protected. Lastly, considering the City of Belval's emphasis on environmental issues and reducing carbon footprint, our company's can propose solutions that incorporate low-carbon impact infrastructures, aligning with the City of Belval's environmental goals while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and maintaining a high level of security." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message10> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, by leveraging our company's experience in EU public procurement, adhering to strict GDPR compliance, protecting intellectual property through work-for-hire models and escrow agreements, ensuring adequate insurance coverage, and promoting environmentally friendly solutions, our company's can effectively mitigate the legal risks associated with this project and provide a compliant, secure, and cost-effective solution for the City of Belval's." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message10> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval has a global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years for this project. Given our pricing model, current financial position, daily rates, overhead, cash position, tender eligibility thresholds, and cost sensitivity parameters as of 2024, what is our projected margin on this project, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose to the client? Based on the provided context, our target gross margin percentage is 28. However, to calculate our projected margin on this contract our need to consider the total contract value and our pricing model. a global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years for this projectt is 3 million euros over 4 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given that our tender eligibility threshold is a maximum contract value of 3 million euros, our are eligible to bid on this project. our current financial position, with an annual revenue of 4.2 million euros and a net profit of 380,000 euros, indicates that our have the capacity to undertake a project of this size. To estimate our costs for this project, our can consider our standard daily rates for various roles, but without specific details on this project requirements and resource allocation, it's challenging to provide an exact cost breakdown. However, assuming our can maintain our projected margin on this contract, our projected revenue from this project would be 3 million euros, and our costs would be such that our costs allow our to achieve a 28% gross margin. our pricing model includes standard daily rates for senior architects, project managers, AI engineers, security engineers, business analysts, junior developers, and change managers. standard daily rates for senior architects, project managers, AI engineers, security engineers, business analysts, junior developers, and change managers range from 550 euros per day for a junior developer to 1,050 euros per day for a senior architect. The infrastructure margin percentage is 12%, and the software license resale margin percentage is 8%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given these parameters, if our were to achieve our target gross margin of 28% on this project, our cost would need to be approximately 2,160,000 euros (3,000,000 * (1 - 0.28)), leaving our with a gross profit of around 840,000 euros. As for cost-optimization strategies, considering our cost sensitivity parameters, our could propose the following to the client: 1. **Absorb costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors**: If the budget were to be reduced by up to 10%, our might be able to absorb some of costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors by renegotiating rates with our subcontractors. 2. **Scope reduction**: For larger budget reductions, up to 20%, our could work with the client to reduce the project scope, removing optional modules or reducing training days, to maintain profitability while still delivering value to the client. 3. **Fundamental scope change for significant budget reductions**: If the budget were to be reduced by more than 30%, our would likely need to fundamentally alter this project scope to make this project viable, which could involve significant changes to the deliverables or the approach taken. By working closely with The City of Belval and understanding The City of Belval specific needs and priorities, our can tailor our proposal to meet The City of Belval budgetary constraints while ensuring this project success and our own financial viability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution should provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents, facilitate access to information, improve quality of answers, reduce processing times, and assist in administrative activities. Considering our company's LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, performance benchmarks, past AI use cases, and known trade-offs as of 2024, what AI components can our company's design to meet these requirements, and how can our company's demonstrate innovation in The solution? To provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents, our company's can leverage our company's LLM stack, specifically the Mistral 7B Instruct model, which is our company's preferred sovereign model due to its strong French-language performance and self-hostable nature. our company's can fine-tune its using our company's LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus to improve its accuracy in answering administrative queries. our company's RAG capabilities can be utilized to facilitate access to information by integrating with existing practices of agents, allowing for quick access to reliable and up-to-date information. The retrieval strategies our company's employ, such as dense vector semantic search or BM25 sparse search, can help improve the quality of answers provided to municipal agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To reduce processing times, our company's can optimize its performance through quantization methods like INT8 or INT4 (GPTQ), which have been shown to use significantly less energy than larger models while maintaining comparable task performance. our company's past experience in deploying AI solutions, such as the regulatory document Q&A assistant and clinical guideline assistant, demonstrates our company's ability to deliver efficient and effective AI-powered tools. In terms of explainability, our company's can employ our company's xAI methods, including source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, or LIME, to provide transparent and understandable recommendations to municipal agents. This is crucial in ensuring that the solution is not only accurate but also trustworthy and compliant with regulatory requirements. To demonstrate innovation in The solution, our company's can highlight our company's current research topics, such as knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning, multi-agent collaboration frameworks, and proactive regulatory change alerting." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By integrating these cutting-edge technologies into our company's AI components, our company's can provide a truly innovative solution that not only meets but exceeds the client's requirements. Furthermore, our company's commitment to minimizing environmental footprint through the use of low-carbon infrastructure and reducing energetic consumption aligns with the client's constraints. our company's experience in deploying solutions that comply with regulatory requirements, such as GDPR, ensures that The solution will meet the necessary standards for data protection and sovereignty. Overall, by combining our company's LLM expertise, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, and commitment to innovation and sustainability, our company's can design an AI-powered solution that provides intelligent assistance to municipal agents while meeting the client's requirements and constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval aims to limit The City of Belval environmental footprint and reduce energetic consumption. Considering our company's EcoVadis rating, carbon footprint, green hosting partners, digital sobriety practices, social commitments, AI ethics principles, and known sustainability trade-offs as of 2024, how can our company's propose a solution that contributes to these goals, and what measures can our company's take to minimize the environmental impact of our company's proposed solution? As the CSR & Sustainability Officer of Nexus Engineering S.r.l., the CSR & Sustainability Officer of Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can propose a solution that aligns with these goals by leveraging Nexus Engineering existing capabilities. Given our company's Silver EcoVadis rating and a score of 62, our company's have a solid foundation in sustainability practices. our company's carbon footprint, with a total scope 1 & 2 of 148 tCO2e as of 2023, indicates an area for improvement, but our company's are working towards net zero by 2040." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To minimize the environmental impact, our proposed solution can utilize green hosting partners like OVHcloud or Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy. utilize directly supports reducing energetic consumption and lowering carbon emissions associated with data hosting. our company's digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy, can also significantly reduce the energy footprint of our proposed solution. For instance, INT8/INT4 model quantisation reduces GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, which is substantial. Furthermore, our company's adhere to strict AI ethics principles that include transparency, human oversight, and no discriminatory outputs. strict AI ethics principles that include transparency, human oversight, and no discriminatory outputs ensure that our proposed solution not only minimizes environmental impact but also contributes positively to social commitments, such as promoting gender equality (with a gender equality index of 88) and accessibility standards like WCAG 2.1 AA. Considering the known sustainability trade-offs, our company's can address tensions between high availability and energy consumption by implementing low-power standby modes that allow for quick wake-up times without significantly compromising our company's SLA requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For on-premise servers, our company's recommend that clients subscribe to renewable energy Guarantee of Origin certificates to ensure clients electricity is sourced from 100% renewable sources. To further minimize environmental impact, our company's can conduct regular carbon reporting (using GRI Standards partially) and aim for an average energy reduction of about 35% compared to our company's baseline. By integrating these practices into our proposed solution, our company's not only contribute to reducing The City of Belval environmental footprint but also demonstrate a commitment to sustainable development and social responsibility." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "# Executive Summary Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with EuroCloud Solutions S.A. and GreenCompute S.r.l., proposes an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in municipal agents of the City of Belval daily administrative tasks. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks leverages cutting-edge technologies, including the Mistral 7B Instruct model for language understanding, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for information retrieval, and a microservices-based architecture for scalability and reliability. # Understanding of Requirements the City of Belval requires an AI-powered solution that can assist municipal agents in accessing reliable and up-to-date information, drafting administrative contents, instructing files, and collaborating with other services. The solution must comply with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, and ensure a high level of security and explicability. # Proposed Solution an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks integrates the following components: 1. **Technical Architecture**: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will design a microservices-based system using containerization (Docker) and orchestration (Kubernetes). Technical Architecture will facilitate flexible scalability, meeting the availability requirement of 99.9%. For integration with existing systems, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will utilize API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, along with API gateways like Kong and Apigee. 2. **AI Components**: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will employ the Mistral 7B Instruct model for language understanding for language understanding, fine-tuned using Nexus Engineering S.r.l. LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. RAG capabilities will be utilized to facilitate access to information by integrating with existing practices of agents. For explainability, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will implement xAI methods such as source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME. 3. **Security and Compliance**: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. hold ISO 27001 certification, which includes the scope of design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. data residency is EU-only, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed. For anonymization, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. use Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. 4. **Budget and Cost Optimization**: Nexus Engineering S.r.l. target gross margin percentage is 28%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. projected revenue from this contract would be 3 million euros, with a required cost of approximately 2,160,000 euros to achieve Nexus Engineering S.r.l. target gross margin. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose cost optimization strategies such as rate renegotiation with subcontractors and scope reduction. 5. **Sustainability**: an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks will utilize green hosting partners like OVHcloud or Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. aim for an average energy reduction of about 35% compared to Nexus Engineering S.r.l. baseline. # Unaddressed Requirements None of the requirements specified by the City of Belval are left unaddressed in proposes. # Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with EuroCloud Solutions S.A. and GreenCompute S.r.l., is confident that an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks meets all the requirements specified by the City of Belval. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. team has the necessary expertise, experience, and capabilities to deliver a high-quality AI-powered solution that assists municipal agents in municipal agents administrative tasks while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and minimizing environmental footprint. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. look forward to the opportunity to discuss proposes in further detail." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval has a global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years for this project, with an annual cost of exploitation that must remain mastered and compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities. The solution should improve the efficiency of administrative services, quality of service rendered to users, reduce environmental footprint, and minimize energetic consumption. Considering our company's PM methodologies, past public sector references, consortium partners, available capacity, and governance practices as of 2024, can our company's assemble a team that meets these requirements and constraints?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

